/// Broad groupings a student achievement falls into.
///
/// Institution-neutral on purpose: these must mean the same thing to every
/// tenant, so nothing here names a competition, a society or a degree. A tenant
/// needing finer granularity uses `title` and `description`, which are free
/// text, rather than expecting this list to grow per university.
enum AchievementCategory {
  ACADEMIC
  SPORTS
  CULTURAL
  TECHNICAL
  RESEARCH
  SOCIAL_SERVICE
  PROFESSIONAL
  OTHER
}

/// Lifecycle of an open-elective offering.
///
/// DRAFT     — being configured. Invisible to students; seats and eligibility
///             may still change.
/// OPEN      — students may submit and EDIT preferences. The only state in
///             which a preference may be written.
/// LOCKED    — preferences frozen. Nothing may be added, changed or withdrawn;
///             the cohort is now fixed and allocation may run against it.
/// ALLOCATED — allocation has run and seats are assigned. Terminal.
///
/// LOCKED precedes ALLOCATED deliberately: freezing the input set before
/// computing against it is what makes an allocation reproducible. Allocating
/// first and locking afterwards would compute against a set that could still
/// move underneath the run.
enum OpenElectiveStatus {
  DRAFT
  OPEN
  LOCKED
  ALLOCATED
}

/// How an offering breaks ties once preference order has been honoured.
///
/// Preference rank is ALWAYS respected first; this decides only what happens
/// between two students competing at the same rank for the last seat.
///
/// FCFS  — the earlier `submittedAt` wins. Cheap and needs nothing beyond the
///         preference row itself.
/// MERIT — the higher CGPA wins, read from the result engine. Undefined for a
///         first-semester student, which the service must handle rather than
///         treating an absent CGPA as zero.
///
/// Stored on the offering because it is CONFIGURATION: two departments in one
/// university may legitimately allocate differently, and neither is the
/// engine's business to choose.
enum ElectiveAllocationStrategy {
  FCFS
  MERIT
}

/// What an allocation run concluded for one student at one offering.
///
/// NOT_ALLOCATED rows are written, not omitted. A student who asked and was
/// refused is the single most important row in an allocation report, and a
/// table that recorded only winners could not answer "why did I not get it".
enum ElectiveAllocationOutcome {
  ALLOCATED
  NOT_ALLOCATED
}

